# Local Engineering Rules

## Verification
- Every agent except the specifier must run unit tests and acceptance tests before handoff and fix any failures.
- The architect, hardender, and QA must run property tests before handoff when the project has them and fix any failures.

## Python Runtime Rules
- Final user-facing executable scripts must use `#!/usr/bin/env -S uv run --script`, an inline dependency declaration, and `requires-python = ">=3.12,<3.14"`.
- Unit tests must mock Mistral, Tavily, and Ollama. Add a separately marked live preflight that calls each configured provider only when the required environment variables and local Ollama service are present.
- Keep network IO in adapters that can be replaced in tests. Do not write generated research data into the source tree except beneath an ignored runtime-output directory.
